t before comparing claims. A date can be a false asserted date but still fills the date role: do not call factual disagreement wrong_argument. Reserve wrong_argument for an actual role/type mismatch. Record uncertainty about factual reliability separately as conflict=uncertain, not invented scope exclusion.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the common name for Yellow Lantern?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 186, \"text\": \"Banksia lemanniana Banksia lemanniana, commonly known as the yellow lantern banksia or Lemann's banksia, is a species of woody shrub of the family Proteaceae native to Western Australia.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 187, \"end\": 328, \"text\": \"It generally grows as an open shrub or small tree to five metres (15 ft) high with stiff serrated leaves, and unusual hanging inflorescences.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 329, \"end\": 488, \"text\": \"Flowering occurs over summer, the greenish buds developing into oval flower spikes before turning grey and developing the characteristic large woody follicles.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 489, \"end\": 593, \"text\": \"It occurs within and just east of the Fitzgerald River National Park on the southern coast of the state.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 594, \"end\": 640, \"text\": \"\\\"Banksia lemanniana\\\" is killed by bushfire and\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 625, \"text\": \"Page information Concept URI Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Create a book Download as PDF Printable version In other projects A